Heap memory - 
	Heap memory is a shared memory area in the JVM where objects and their associated instance data are generally allocated. It is managed by the Garbage Collector, which removes objects that are no longer reachable.
	
Why Do We Need Heap Memory?
	Objects often need to live longer than a single method call.
	
other definition - Heap memory is a JVM memory area shared among threads where objects and their instance data are generally allocated. It is managed by the Garbage Collector, which can reclaim memory from objects that are no longer reachable. Unlike stack memory, which is per-thread and stores method execution frames, heap memory is shared and primarily stores dynamically created objects.

