open closed principle - 
	Software entities such as classes, modules, and functions should be open for extension but closed for modification.

most common to implement ocp is interfaces.

Design the code so that new kinds of behavior can usually be added through extension rather than repeatedly modifying stable existing code.

OCP can be achieved using: Interfaces, Inheritance, composition, polymorphism, strategy pattern, dependency injection.

other defintion - The Open/Closed Principle states that software entities should be open for extension but closed for modification. We should design classes so that new behavior can be added without repeatedly changing existing, stable code. In Java, this is commonly achieved using interfaces or abstract classes with polymorphism.

